WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.112
This is an optional integration project that combines JOIN thinking with a technique from earlier SQL work.

00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:14.492
The common table expression creates a patient timeline by stacking admissions, lab tests,

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:14.812
and prescriptions with UNION ALL.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:23.217
Each source is transformed into the same basic shape: patient ID, event date, event type, and event details.

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:26.242
At that stage, the grain is one event.

00:00:26.242 --> 00:00:33.477
Then we join the event stream to patients using patient ID so each event can include the patient's

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:37.892
name. The join enriches the event rows without changing the event grain.

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:40.957
This pattern is useful in many real projects.

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:47.637
A customer journey could combine orders, website visits, support calls, and returns.

00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:54.417
A student timeline could combine registrations, submissions, advising appointments, and logins.

00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:58.647
Run the query and follow one patient across several dates.

00:00:58.647 --> 00:01:04.757
The main Module 6 lesson is to notice how clearly defining the event grain before the join makes

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:08.454
the final result easier to understand and validate.
